 Storage Engine Details
 &lt;a class="anchor" href="#storage-engine-details">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>Centralized storage data is centralized, and the amount of data involved is larger, making the data more vulnerable to attacks and leaks. The security, privacy and sustainability of centrally stored data all present certain risks.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Data security includes two meanings: the first layer is &amp;ldquo;guarantee data privacy without leakage&amp;rdquo;, and the second layer is &amp;ldquo;guarantee the integrity of data without loss&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>In the current centralized storage mode, users upload all sensitive data, which not only makes users lose control over their own data, but also transfers the risk of data leakage to the cloud storage operator. If the private information is lost, damaged, leaked, or stolen, it may cause heavy losses to individuals, enterprises and even the entire society.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Protocol</title><link>https://flowshield.icefirelabs.xyz/flowshield_docs/cloudslit/cloudslit-client/architecture/protocol/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://flowshield.icefirelabs.xyz/flowshield_docs/cloudslit/cloudslit-client/architecture/protocol/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="protocol-details">
