&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>Current certificate systems protect online communications through the secure delivery of public keys, which correspond to identities, which use the corresponding secret private key to decrypt messages sent to them and prove that they sent messages (by signing them with the private key). Additionally users cannot be sure that their communications have not been compromised by fraudulent certificates that allow MITM (man-in-the-middle) attacks, which are difficult to detect.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>